; getline_negative_index: the other half of the same bound.
;
; The two halves are reached by different code -- the usize conversion
; rejects this one and the extent comparison rejects
; getline_index_out_of_range's -- so both are pinned. They must report the
; same identity, and both must report the raw operand rather than whatever
; the conversion produced.
;
; A lookup that simply missed on a negative key would return 0 here.

PUSH 4
BQMX r0

PUSH -1
GETLINE r0
HALT
